.TH FORGEKIT 1 "2026-08-25" "ForgeKit 0.3.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
forgekit \- Go CLI for generating, managing, analyzing and diagnosing backend APIs
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B forgekit
[\fIcommand\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ForgeKit
is a developer CLI written in Go that helps you bootstrap backend REST APIs
without manually creating the same project structure, configuration, database
integration, Docker files, migrations, and tests every time.

It generates production-ready Go REST APIs with a clean hexagonal architecture,
including PostgreSQL integration, Docker Compose, database migrations,
environment configuration, and automatic tests.

ForgeKit also provides a feature system to extend generated projects with
additional capabilities (authentication, CORS, logging, Swagger/OpenAPI),
and validation tools to ensure architectural compliance.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Initialize a new ForgeKit project
.TP
.B add
Add a feature to an existing project
.TP
.B remove
Remove a feature from an existing project
.TP
.B analyze
Analyze the project structure and practices
.TP
.B check
Validate architectural conventions
.TP
.B doctor
Diagnose the development environment and project health
.TP
.B inspect
Inspect the ForgeKit project signature
.TP
.B remove
Remove a feature from an existing project
.TP
.B version
Print version information
.TP
.B config
Manage ForgeKit configuration
.TP
.B completion
Generate shell completion scripts
.TP
.B help
Show help for any command
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable debug output
.TP
.B \-\-format \fIformat\fR
Output format: human, json (default: human)
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Reduce output (except errors and JSON)
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Initialize a new project interactively:
.B forgekit init my-api
.TP
Initialize non-interactively:
.B forgekit init my-api --module github.com/example/my-api --port 8080 --non-interactive
.TP
List available features:
.B forgekit add --list
.TP
Install a feature with preview:
.B forgekit add auth --plan
.TP
Install a feature:
.B forgekit add auth
.TP
Analyze project in CI mode:
.B forgekit analyze --ci
.TP
Check project health:
.B forgekit doctor
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
Error or warning (in CI mode)
.TP
.B 2
Execution error
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.forgekit/config.yaml
User configuration
.TP
.I ./forge.yaml
Project configuration
.TP
.I ./.forge/features.yaml
Installed features tracking
